        "Enrico Costa",
        "Filippo Frontera",
        "Shrinivas R. Kulkarni"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Afterglow localization established gamma-ray bursts as cosmological explosions and enabled a major branch of time-domain astrophysics.",
        "attribution": "Costa and Frontera were pivotal in the BeppoSAX breakthrough, with Kulkarni central to optical follow-up and interpretation.",
        "maturity": "The cosmological origin and broad physical importance of gamma-ray bursts are firmly established.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery depended on rapid multi-observatory follow-up, making the allocation of a three-person prize difficult."
        ]
      }
    }
